# Copy this file to `.env` if you need to override anything:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. The presentation editor runs without one;
# the optional chord agent requires the credentials documented below.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle at build time,
# so never put a secret in one.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stem separation. Overrides where the ~172MB Demucs ONNX model is fetched
# from — self-host it, or point at a different export. The default is a public
# Hugging Face copy, cached in the browser after the first download.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_DEMUCS_MODEL_URL=https://example.com/htdemucs_embedded.onnx

# Ultimate Guitar agent — read ONLY by the local Node service.
# These settings are required for the agent, not for the presentation editor.
# Never prefix these secrets with VITE_. Do not overwrite an existing .env.
# Song identification runs on OpenRouter free models (no payment method needed,
# 20 requests/min and 50/day). Any OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions endpoint works.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# UG_AGENT_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free
# Transcription still uses OpenAI.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ULTIMATE_GUITAR_USERNAME=
# ULTIMATE_GUITAR_PASSWORD=
# Speech-to-text used to time the slides to the song (the MP3 is sent to OpenAI).
# Must support verbose_json segment timestamps. Default: whisper-1.
# UG_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=whisper-1
# Optional: false opens a visible Chromium window for login/CAPTCHA/OTP.
# The default is visible on desktop and headless on Linux without a display.
# UG_HEADLESS=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub credentials for the agent team do NOT belong in this file.
#
# Two reasons:
#
# 1. `gh` and `git` read GH_TOKEN from the shell environment. This file is
#    loaded by dotenv inside the Node service (server/ug/config.ts) — putting a
#    token here would not authenticate `gh` at all.
#
# 2. The pm seat and the dev/review seats hold DIFFERENT tokens with different
#    permissions. A single file sourced by every pane would give the dev seat
#    pm's master-capable token, which defeats the separation entirely.
#
# They live outside the repo, one per seat:
#
#     ~/.herdr/pm.env       # pm only:    contents+PR+issues write, actions read
#     ~/.herdr/agent.env    # dev/review: contents write, issues read
#
# Neither file holds a token. Each one only exports GH_CONFIG_DIR, pointing gh
# at that seat's own config directory where `gh auth login` stored the PAT —
# so no token ever sits in the shell environment, where /proc, subprocesses and
# any stray `env` dump would expose it. Source the matching one per pane:
#
#     . ~/.herdr/<seat>.env
#
# Each file also documents the exact fine-grained PAT permissions to grant.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
